PAC-MAN V3 - C++ OFFLINE CONSOLE GAME
=====================================

PROJECT RULES
-------------
- C++ only (C++11 or later).
- Designed for Windows with MinGW/GCC.
- Runs offline. No API keys, internet, cloud services or online assets.
- Exactly 8 project files are included in this ZIP.
- Includes original synthesized arcade-style gameplay sounds, played asynchronously without blocking movement or triggering Windows error beeps.
- Emoji graphics require a UTF-8 capable terminal and a font with emoji support.
- scores.txt is created automatically in the game folder when a game ends.

FILES (EXACTLY 8)
-----------------
game.cpp    Main game loop, lives, levels, countdown, pause, collisions and victory.
game.h      Shared enums, structures and function declarations.
player.cpp  Keyboard input, movement, coin/power pellet collection.
ghost.cpp   Ghost movement, chase/scatter/frightened behaviour and personalities.
maze.cpp    Maze layouts, emoji rendering, walls, coins and power pellets.
menu.cpp    Main menu, instructions, difficulty and sound settings.
records.cpp Top 10 leaderboard and local player statistics.
README     Project documentation and build instructions.

FEATURES
--------
1. Three lives per game.
2. Power pellets and temporary frightened ghost behaviour.
3. Three progressive levels.
4. Bonus fruit and bonus points.
5. Easy, Medium and Hard difficulty.
6. Chase, scatter and frightened ghost modes.
7. Three ghost movement personalities.
8. Wall-aware ghost movement.
9. Pause and resume with P.
10. Three-second start countdown.
11. Game-over and victory screens.
12. HUD for score, lives, level, coins, difficulty, sound and power.
13. Emoji graphics for player, ghosts, walls, coins, power and fruit.
14. Top 10 local leaderboard.
15. Local player statistics.
16. Persistent scores in scores.txt.
17. High score ranking through leaderboard sorting.
18. Original synthesized arcade sound effects for coin collection, power pellets, ghost collisions, fruit and game results.
19. Sound ON/OFF option.
20. New all-time high-score notification.
21. No internet or API keys required.

CONTROLS
--------
W / Up Arrow       Move up
A / Left Arrow     Move left
S / Down Arrow     Move down
D / Right Arrow    Move right
P                  Pause / resume
Q                  Quit current game

BUILD (WINDOWS / MINGW)
-----------------------
Open CMD in the folder containing the 6 .cpp files and game.h, then run:

g++ game.cpp player.cpp ghost.cpp maze.cpp menu.cpp records.cpp -o PacMan.exe -std=c++11 -lwinmm

RUN
---
PacMan.exe

NOTES
-----
- Sound is generated locally as short PCM WAV tones and played asynchronously with Windows PlaySound; compile with -lwinmm.
- Sound can be enabled or disabled from the main menu. No external sound files are required.
- Use Windows Terminal or a UTF-8 enabled terminal for best emoji display.
- Emoji glyph widths vary by terminal/font; if alignment looks unusual, use a
  terminal with emoji support.
- scores.txt is runtime data and is intentionally not included in the ZIP.
- The ZIP contains only the eight named project files.
